    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on targeting mid-tier pitching to bolster our counting stats, led by our most potent play, **Kyle Tucker** (78.68). Facing Randy V\u00e1squez, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a favorable matchup environment, making him the anchor of our outfield. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** (68.05) offers elite utility against Aaron Civale; his 14% dynamic platoon advantage confirms his status as a premier start, while **Josh Jung** (66.29) remains a strong play against Kyle Freeland, buoyed by a significant 14% park factor boost at Coors Field. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (51.15) carry lower scores than usual due to SP skill dampeners and dynamic platoon disadvantages, their elite skill profiles necessitate their inclusion in our daily rotation to maintain our floor.\n\nThe tightest decision on the bench involved **Miguel Vargas** (50.12), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Gage Workman** (50.95). While **Miguel Vargas** offers excellent utility, the optimizer favored **Gage Workman**'s specific platoon edge against Tanner Bibee. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Jackson Merrill** (49.37), who was relegated to the bench primarily because of the overwhelming difficulty presented by Shohei Ohtani\u2019s 2.75 xERA. It is critical to note that all scores remain \"Lineup Pending\" projections; any defensive shifts or late-scratches could materially alter the efficiency scores for **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, both of whom are heavily reliant on their assumed spots at the top and bottom of the order to provide value. We are prioritizing volume today, but remain ready to pull back on **Nolan Schanuel** or **Sam Antonacci** if weather or late-breaking lineup changes compromise their projected plate appearances.",
